
- **Trustees & AMC:** high integrity and fairness in all dealings
- Schemes not run in interest of sponsors, AMC/trustee directors or associates
- Equitable, fair treatment of all classes of unitholders
- Adequate, accurate, timely information in simple language
- Avoid excessive concentration with brokers/associates and of units among few investors; avoid conflicts of interest
- Each scheme''s assets, liabilities, bank & securities accounts ring-fenced
- Invest per stated objectives, solely in unitholders'' interest; no unethical selling
- High service standards, due diligence, independent judgment; no exaggerated claims
- Advice in public media only with disclosure of own (and family/employer) positions
- Regulated entities & agents (incl. MFDs) must show registered name & number on social media home page and at start of each video/content

## Appendix 2: AMFI Code of Ethics (1/2)

- **Integrity:** fair dealings; schemes not run for sponsors, directors, trustees, brokers, associates or a special class of unitholders
- **Due diligence:** high service standards, independent judgment, adequate resources
- Disclosures:
  - Timely, simple information on objectives, policies, financials
  - Annual disclosure of investment pattern, portfolio, expense ratios, portfolio turnover
  - Deals with associates/significant unitholders (≥ 5% of corpus) – justify to trustees; disclose in annual & half-yearly reports
  - Key investment personnel''s trades reported to compliance officer at least half-yearly
- **Professional selling:** no unethical means or exaggerated performance claims; disclose risks; provide literature; fair allotment & prompt refunds; handle complaints
  - Don''t present scheme as a share issue, create unrealistic expectations, guarantee returns (unless in SID), offer extraneous benefits or misrepresent

## Appendix 2: AMFI Code of Ethics (2/2)

- **Investment practices:** follow SID objectives; no trades with own directors/officers/employees or trustees
- Operations – prohibited:
  - Front running (trading ahead of fund using non-public information)
  - Self-dealing (benefiting at the fund''s expense)
  - Fraudulent, deceptive or manipulative practices; false markets, price rigging, passing price-sensitive information
  - Staff acting as agents for own schemes (except as employees)
  - Changing fundamental attributes without unitholder approval (unless due to regulation)
- **Reporting:** standard valuation; total-return performance reporting; scheme-wise segregation of cash & securities
- No unfair competition; observe letter and spirit of law
